From 938d4738c11924229ddd72d3dcb5328c8da11a0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D. Zack Garza" <dzackgarza@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:23:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/16] fix: keep the image's Julia depot on the bridge's path

sage-julia-bridge launches julia with --project=<checkout>/julia_env, whose
Project.toml requires JSON and Oscar, and imports JSON in its first statement.
Those packages are installed in /opt/julia-depot, declared by the image's own
JULIA_DEPOT_PATH. A container runtime applies that declaration to every
process; a host that runs the unpacked filesystem instead -- PRoot, a bare
exec, an entrypoint that rebuilds the environment -- starts the bridge without
it, Julia falls back to ~/.julia, and the bridge aborts at julia_bridge.jl:2
with "Package JSON [682c06a0-de6a-54ab-a142-c8b1cf79cde6] is required but does
not seem installed: Run Pkg.instantiate()". That ArgumentError is reproducible
in this image by removing JULIA_DEPOT_PATH and starting the bridge.

/usr/local/bin/julia becomes the image's launcher rather than a symlink to
/opt/julia/bin/julia: it adds /opt/julia-depot to whatever depot path the
caller has, once, and execs the real binary. Every consumer reaches Julia
through PATH, so none of them installs JSON, Oscar or anything else for itself.

The image check now starts the bridge with JULIA_DEPOT_PATH removed and
asserts a JSON call through it, and asserts the same call on the session it
already holds: the first fails on the image as published, the second pins the
worker project's own dependency rather than the default environment's.

Not touched: the research repository pins in docker/research-repositories.txt.
The embedded port revision and the post-move research revision are not a
verified pair, and the port project is moving to canonical sage_extensions.
